# UI quality

Nii Plants must feel modern, premium, warm, and Ghanaian without clichés. Do not ship a generic shadcn template, a black-and-gold supercar look, or default Inter/Geist marketing pages.

shadcn components are primitives. After adding one, restyle spacing, type, states, and composition to match the project tokens in `src/app/globals.css`.

Required on every user-facing surface:

- Mobile-first layouts that still work at 360px, tablet, and desktop
- Clear typography hierarchy (display font for major titles, interface font for UI)
- Consistent spacing, selective radius, simple shadows, clearly defined cards
- Hover, focus-visible, disabled, loading, empty, and error states
- Accessible names, labels, keyboard support, and contrast
- `next/image` for photographs; no huge autoplay video

After UI changes, inspect the actual page in a browser (Playwright or the running app). Do not claim visual quality from code inspection alone.

Do not invent prices, phone numbers, fleet, reviews, or other live business facts. Use labelled placeholders.
